  "excitation_report": "Backbone = isentropic area-Mach relation: g = -Ar + (1/M)[(2/(gam+1))(1+(gam-1)/2 M^2)]^((gam+1)/(2(gam-1))), whose root gives the subsonic M(Ar). Terms are perturbations; visibility judged as delta-M ~ -term/F'(M0) with |F'|~2.5, sigma=0.003. NOTE: auto_balance/excitation_check ran in 'explicit' mode and left M unbound (all M-dependent terms returned NaN; only -Ar evaluated at 420*sigma) because the tools do not root-solve the implicit relation where M cancels from both sides -> per-term multiples were computed analytically instead. NEW term (Csep separation, E-parent): in g it reaches ~0.13-0.16 with pback/p0=1.3, i.e. delta-M ~ 0.05-0.06 ~ 17-21*sigma across the range -> strongly visible. Legacy corrections peak near the throat (low Ar / high M), included via Ar starting at 1.02: friction Cf term ~4.8*sigma at M~0.5 (grows with Ar*log Ar); heat Qh term up to ~4.4*sigma near throat; Kre back-pressure term up to ~4*sigma near throat. All terms exceed 5*sigma somewhere in the sampled region except heat/Kre which sit ~1-1.5*sigma at the high-Ar end but are clearly excited near Ar~1.02.",
