  "rationale": "The record is M = M + (...), so M cancels and the relation is IMPLICIT: g(M; Ar, params)=0, not explicitly solvable for M (analyze_expression: no derivatives, no integrals, explicitly_solvable_for_target=false). Solve M by root-finding at each Ar. Ar (area ratio A/A*) is the only physical axis for 'M vs area ratio in the subsonic branch'; gam, Tw, pback were labeled as axes but are fixed gas/boundary constants and were fixed as parameters. Ar in [1.02,3.0] traces the subsonic branch (M from ~0.85 down to ~0.2), avoiding the M=1 sonic point at Ar=1. Parameters chosen at plausible magnitudes; Cf and Kre raised toward the top of a plausible lumped-coefficient range and pback/p0=1.3 set to activate the separation tanh so the NEW separation term is well above noise. Tools could not evaluate M-dependent terms for this implicit case (M left unbound in 'explicit' mode); excitation was therefore assessed analytically and the new term is comfortably visible.",
